  "body": "## What changed\n\n- 2D Contour takes \"Do not touch\" protected faces and edges (`do_not_touch_applies`). The Boundary group of a Contour shows \"Pick protected\", and a viewport click adds a face row or an edge row.\n- Each Contour mode has an avoid-aware twin in `camcraft-motion` (`contour_avoid*` modules):\n  - closed rings, rings on a part, picked rings;\n  - the whole-model contour;\n  - open chains, open runs on the part side and on the stock side;\n  - DXF sketch loops and chains (`contour_sketch.rs`).\n- Each twin keeps the flutes, the shank and the holder clear of each protected item, by the clearance. This applies to cuts, leads, links and plunges.\n- A ring is clipped at each level against the keep-out of the full tool. The kept pieces are cut as open pieces. A lead, a link or an entry that enters the keep-out is dropped or moved.\n- A ring or a chain that is blocked on every level is skipped. A note names the protected items. When no cut remains, the operation is refused, and the refusal names the items. Control compensation that a clip would break is refused by name.\n- Each result goes through the full-tool verify before it leaves the generator. The app verify and the post gate read the Contour moves as they read the other kinds (`verify_avoid`).\n- With no protected item, each twin calls the plain generator. The toolpath does not change.\n- The MCP tool text and `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` list 2D Contour.\n\nThis PR resumes the held branch of 2026-11-22 (1993c0cf1). That work was never built. The merge of main needed these changes:\n\n- Ports into the avoid emitter of what main changed in `contour::emit_band`: the ring entry (#3830, #3917), the pecked dive (#3678), the picked seam under compensation (#1473), the tab level start (#3453), the picked ladder, and the start/exit picks that moved to `ContourParams::picks`.\n- Two real defects in the held code, found by the pins:\n  - A clipped piece ended on the keep-out boundary. `Region::contains` counts the boundary as inside. Each piece without a lead read as blocked and was dropped, so a bore with a protected pin cut nothing. Fix: the piece ends step 0.001 mm back (`END_TRIM`).\n  - A bore-side piece entry fell back to the whole centre region, without the keep-out. The entry dived beside the protected pin, and the shank came 0.83 mm short of the clearance. The final verify refused it, so no G-code was wrong. Fix: the entry room is always the centre less the keep-out; an entry point outside it grazes at itself.\n\n## Cause\n\n`do_not_touch_applies` did not list `OpType::Contour`, and the Contour generators had no keep-out law.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (all red before the change, green after):\n\n- `camcraft-motion --test avoid_contour`:\n  - `empty_avoid_matches_plain_contour_paths_exactly`\n  - `contour_avoid_closed_partial_tabs_inside_whole_and_open_stay_clear`\n  - `contour_avoid_refuses_unavoidable_control_and_blocked_pick_by_name`\n- `camcraft-app --test do_not_touch` (new submodule `do_not_touch/contour.rs`):\n  - `contour::contour_do_not_touch_keeps_full_tool_clear_of_protected_face_and_edge` (no posted move nearer than the clearance, checked on the NC)\n  - `contour::contour_do_not_touch_refuses_unavoidable_cut_and_blocks_post` (refusal names the item; post blocked; no NC file)\n  - `contour::contour_without_do_not_touch_keeps_same_toolpath` (same NC with and without an empty protection)\n  - `contour::contour_modes_picked_open_and_dxf_sketch_stay_clear`\n- `camcraft-ui --lib`:\n  - `egui_app::tests::do_not_touch::contour_shows_pick_protected_and_no_unsupported_note`\n  - `egui_app::tests::do_not_touch_click::contour_takes_a_protected_face_and_edge_by_viewport_click`\n\nMutation checks (each guard put back to the old code, pins run, then restored):\n\n- M1 `do_not_touch_applies` without Contour: 3 app pins red, 2 UI pins red. The baseline pin stays green.\n- M2 no `END_TRIM` step: `contour_avoid_closed_partial_...` red (\"no safe cutting room remains\").\n- M3 bore entry falls back to the whole centre: `contour_avoid_closed_partial_...` red (shank 0.829 mm short).\n- M4 the Contour dispatch in `generate.rs` ignores protection: 3 app pins red (gouges, missing refusal). The baseline pin stays green.\n\nExpected-change tests:\n\n- `pocket3d_do_not_touch_keeps_clear_raises_links_and_blocks_impossible_cut` used a Contour as its unsupported kind. It uses a Slot now, and the message check also reads \"2D Contour\".\n- The UI test `unsupported_op_shows_do_not_touch_note_without_pick_button` used a Contour. Each kind that has a Boundary group now takes protection, so no kind shows that note in the UI. The test is now `contour_shows_pick_protected_and_no_unsupported_note`. The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by one.\n\nFixture changes in the new pins, with the reason:\n\n- The shared fixture's stock is 24 mm tall, and the pins cut the plate at Z 10..5. Main's flute law (#3525) blocks a 15 mm flute there, with or without protection. The pins edit the tool to a 25 mm flute and a 2 mm shank. The holder base stays at tip + 27 mm.\n- The NC check measures the true 3D gap of each tool band to the protected box.\n- The plain tilted (3+2) Contour and the plain sketch Contour of the fixture already have gouge and crossing findings on main. For those two cases the pins check only what protection adds: no `avoid_hit`, and (sketch) no finding kind that the plain path lacks.\n\nCommands on the final head (c50a967e8):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 339 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (37.8 min). It includes `ui suites: lib`, where the two UI pins ran and passed on this box.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The quick gate ran `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` and `golden_cl`: green.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` reaches 111 steps (the app and motion heavy lanes). AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" (#3556) gives a P3 PR no heavy step; the light lane is the review's step.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff changes no `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file, and the catalog and golden suites above are green.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The tilted (3+2) Contour with protection gets a `rapid_in_part` finding that the plain tilted path does not have. The plain tilted path already has gouge findings in this fixture, so the post is blocked in both cases. Follow-up: #4131.\n- No \"incomplete\" operation status exists. A blocked ring or chain is skipped with a named note, as Bore and the Pocket and Trace protection do. See `docs/decisions/3344-contour-do-not-touch.md`.\n- No UI screenshots: the change shows an existing button for one more kind. The UI pins assert the button and the viewport clicks.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nOpen PRs that touch the same files, different functions or rows; whichever merges second refreshes:\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: #4050, #4028, #4008, #3832, #3103 (other operation arms; this PR changes the Contour arm only).\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/mod.rs`: #4028, #4008, #3103 (module and `pub use` lists).\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`: #4050, #3963 (other tool rows).\n\nNew top-level test file: `crates/motion/tests/avoid_contour.rs`. Reason: `crates/motion/tests/` has no directory suite for the avoid laws; its siblings `avoid_pocket.rs`, `avoid_adaptive.rs` and `avoid_engrave.rs` are top-level files too. The app pins joined the `do_not_touch` directory suite.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: 2D Contour takes \"Do not touch\" faces and edges: the full tool stays clear of them on cuts, leads, links and plunges, and a cut that cannot keep clear is refused by name.\n\nFixes #3344\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
